 "design_names_realized_as": {
  "scanCE, finishCE, run_scanCE (8.3 step 2)": "as designed, with scanCE_finish and the equations scanCE_pure, scanCE_accept_zero, scanCE_accept_succ, scanCE_other",
  "compile_scan (8.3 step 2)": "compile_scan with compileCut (item 2's AcceptCut.scan of the compiled program is the compiled CE scan); compile_noAccept, scan_query_other, scan_bind_noAccept",
  "pool registration handler, create_merge_pool, step_merge_pool, compile_simulation_pool (8.3 step 3, P-a layer 1)": "handlerPool, revealPool, deploymentPool, compiledPool, create_merge_pool, step_merge_pool, compile_simulation_pool, good_create_pool, good_step_pool, compile_native_pool",
  "pool variants of compile_game / initialized_native (P-a layer 2)": "not built; the constructor link is made once in ideal_prefix and item2_prefix from item 2's annotated birth",
  "pool variants of the initialization layers down to KemInitialization.commands, closed by DynamicKemJointSource.program_source (P-a layer 3)": "PqxdhDeploymentIdealPoolSource: programPool_native (erasure), program_reserved (encoding), stopped_program (router, exact), kemCommands_stopped",
  "exposeAt_scan, scan_opaque, preRaw_opaque to sourcePreOpaque's context (8.3 step 3 glue)": "not needed: item2_prefix is stated on PqxdhDeploymentIdealParams.preOpaquePool (the opaque prephase at a given family)",
  "prefix_compile (8.3)": "ideal_prefix (CE side) and item2_prefix (item 2's side) over the common prefix commonPrefix, with ideal_cut, pool_scan_source, stopped_scan_source",
  "CutRel (8.3 step 4)": "CutRel with cut_rel (cut_owned, cut_good, cut_prefix) on every outcome of commonPrefix, at the scan output; owner j holds pool entry j as cut_entry_key (PoolIndexed, cut_indexed), a separate lemma (review fix pass)",
  "no run stops, the budget (8.4)": "at the cut: cut_residual (scan_residual, sourcePool_keys), the continuation's remaining creation budget from the whole compiled program's budget (review fix pass); the rest is U6"
 },
 "deviations_from_design": [
  "route P-a layer 2 (CE-3 game wrappers for the pool) not built: the Server construction is item 2's annotated birth on both sides",
  "glue through exposeAt_scan, scan_opaque and preRaw_opaque not needed: item 2's side stated on preOpaquePool",
  "router step proved exactly against the stopped selected-first router (routerOf), not through DynamicKemJointSource.program_source (projected, normal router)",
  "both prefixes are images of one computation (commonPrefix) rather than a coupling of two prefixes",
  "the relation at the cut sits at the scan output, before the selected accept's verification; the steps before encapsulation move to U6's accept step (+0.25-0.5 to U6)",
  "idealRun_unghost (the LQ-F ghosts never steer the ideal handler) added, so the CE state at the cut is a function of the deployment state (cutState)",
  "the source budget of item 2's scan of the compiled program is a premise of item2_prefix, stopped_scan_source, cut_prefix, cut_rel and cut_entry_key; cut_residual takes the source budget of the whole compiled program (implies the scan budget by AcceptCut.scan_bound; CE-9 compile_full_certified gives it); instantiation from the CE budget is left to ideal_compile (U6)",
  "cut_residual and cut_indexed/cut_entry_key are separate lemmas, not CutRel fields, so cut_rel keeps its premises (review fix pass)",
  "third layer in its own registered module PqxdhDeploymentIdealPoolSource (design-v2 section 11 lists IdealCut and IdealPool)",
  "slotImpl_lift and slotCore_lift publish increment 2's scratch slotImpl_coins and slotCore_onSlots in U5's namespace (U2 runs in parallel); U2's PqxdhDeploymentIdealErase.slotImpl_coins (same statement as slotImpl_lift) and slotCore_onSlots (overlaps slotCore_lift), on codex/deployment-ce11b since 2f46f1a5, are canonical for later units; the U5 copies stay"
 ],
